course: dictionary
lesson: 4388
title: Words from the deep sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hagfish is a sea creature you may never have met, so the words around it will help. «Hagfish make huge amounts of slime when attacked» tells you that hagfish are attacked, and that they make slime when they are. You can work out much of the meaning from clues like these before you check a dictionary.
explain: Look for clues about what kind of thing a word is. «The hagfish is an eel-shaped fish with no jaws» tells you it is a fish, and that its long body is like an eel's. Hagfish is a noun, a naming word for a creature: one hagfish, two hagfish.
explain: Science texts often use a word in several sentences, and each sentence adds a clue. «It eats dead animals» and «it helps clean the sea floor» together show what a scavenger is: an animal that eats dead things. Put the clues together, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A hagfish is a long, eel-shaped sea fish with no jaws that lives on the deep sea floor.
fact: «Scavenger» means an animal that eats dead animals.
fact: «Slime» means a thick, slippery goo; a hagfish can make enough to fill a bucket in seconds.
fact: «Hagfish» can make slime that clogs an attacker's gills, which is a strange way to defend itself.
exercise: «Hagfish make huge amounts of slime when attacked.» What does slime mean here? | *A thick, slippery goo | A hard shell | Sand from the sea floor | A sticky sweet
exercise: «The hagfish is an eel-shaped fish with no jaws.» What does eel-shaped tell you? | Short and furry | Made of metal | *Long and thin, like an eel | Round and flat, like a plate
exercise: «A hagfish helps clean the sea floor by eating dead whales and fish.» What does this tell you about what a hagfish eats? | It eats rocks | It eats only plants | *It eats dead animals | It eats live fish that swim fast
test: «When attacked, it ties itself in a knot to wipe the slime off.» What does the hagfish do to wipe off the slime? | *It ties its body into a knot | It calls for help | It swims away very fast | It rubs against a rock
test: «It can live for months without eating.» What does months tell you about the hagfish? | It only lives for one day | It needs food every minute | *It can go a long time without food | It eats every hour
exam: «When a whale dies and sinks, crabs, hagfish and sleeper sharks eat the meat.» Which animals eat the whale? | Nobody, the whale is too big | Only the worms | Dolphins and seals | *Crabs, hagfish and sleeper sharks
